      "edit_width": "Per-row int; equals len(original) - len(replacement). For substitution edits (e.g., Lean.Parser.*) this is the local byte savings of the rewrite. For deletion edits (kind starts with 'cleanup_' or equals 'dead_have'), the replacement is the empty string and edit_width equals len(original). Prefer this field over the per-row 'savings' field for RL reward shaping; 'savings' is heterogeneous across kinds and 'bytes_original'/'bytes_shortened' are whole-file counters that repeat across rows of the same file.",
      "union_schema_normalisation": "Within each shard, training_pairs and rejected_pairs share a single union schema; fields not produced by a given pipeline are emitted as JSON null. Required for HuggingFace parquet auto-conversion.",
      "always_null_dropped": "Per-split union schema. Columns that were 100% null within a split have been dropped from that split's files (no information loss). Training: err_msg/wall_ms are not emitted (training rows are accepted; failure metadata is by definition rejected-only). Rejected: failed_attempts/failed_tactics are not emitted (these are only populated for the winning attempt of a tournament). See per-split feature schemas in README dataset_info.",
